    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leading the charge at a 65.32 efficiency score. His matchup against Gray is boosted significantly by favorable wind conditions (+10%) and an advantageous spot in the #2 hole, making him our primary engine for R and RBI production. **Gunnar Henderson** (62.18) also presents as an elite option despite facing a tough arm in Bryan Woo; the dynamic platoon advantage against a righty is simply too valuable to ignore. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** continues to provide high-floor consistency at 60.70, anchored by a park factor that plays well for his profile. \n\nWhile the optimizer favored our top-line starters, **Josh Jung** (42.87) was the most difficult exclusion from the daily lineup. He fell just short of the 44-point threshold required to displace lower-scoring options like **Sam Antonacci** or **Brayan Rocchio**, largely due to a harsh SP skill penalty (-18%) against Joe Ryan. We are also monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Drake Baldwin**, **Nolan Schanuel**, and **Miguel Vargas**; while their projected scores are solid, any shift in batting order could volatility impact their output. **Miguel Vargas** remains a speculative value play, as the slow delivery of Ryan Weathers keeps his stolen base potential higher than usual (+2%), providing a much-needed boost in our scarcest category. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given the density of left-on-left matchups facing **Nolan Schanuel**, **Brayan Rocchio**, and **Sam Antonacci**. While **Sam Antonacci** occupies the lineup, his sub-42 score reflects the difficulty of a platoon disadvantage at the bottom of the order. We are holding **Kyle Tucker** in reserve today due to his scheduled day off, but we remain prepared to adjust the roster should any late-breaking lineup changes affect the availability of key assets like **Dominic Smith** or **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**.",
